          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Be the first player or team to reach exactly 61 points by making the open ends of the layout total multiples of 3 or 5 (and optionally scoring for chipping out).',
          gameplay: 'First hand starter is determined by lot (e.g. each draws a tile, highest starts); in later hands the turn to start passes left. Play is clockwise. Each turn a player adds one tile to an end of the layout, matching the inward end of the played tile to the outward end of the tile it touches; doubles are placed crosswise and count as the total of their pips when at an open end. A player who cannot play must knock and the turn passes. The hand ends when one player chips out (plays their last tile) or all players are blocked; in the four-player partnership game both members of one team must chip out. After each play the two open ends are totalled: if the total is a multiple of 5, 3 or both, the player scores immediately (e.g. 3→1, 5→1, 6→2, 9→3, 10→2, 12→4, 15→8, 18→6, 20→4). Chip-out scores 1 point. First to exactly 61 wins; a score that would exceed 61 is disregarded.',
          keyRules: [
            'Score when open ends total a multiple of 3 or 5 (or both); possible scores 3→1, 5→1, 6→2, 9→3, 10→2, 12→4, 15→8, 18→6, 20→4.',
            'Doubles at an end count as the sum of their pips for scoring.',
            'Cannot draw from the boneyard; must play a matching tile or knock.',
            'First to exactly 61 wins; going over 61 that deal is disregarded and a new hand is played.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Track which tiles have been played; the player who can count outstanding tiles has an advantage.',
          intermediate: 'Note numbers on which an opponent was unable to play to infer their hand and block scoring opportunities.',
          advanced: 'Valuable tiles that move one scoring position to another: 0-3, 1-4, 2-5, 3-6, double 3, and double 6; use them to set up or deny multiples of 3 and 5.',
          tips: [
            'Doubles at an end count as the sum of their pips; double 5 and a 5 at the other end make 15 (8 points).',
            'In partnership play both members of a team must chip out to end the hand.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
